(6820106, 1025828, 15711, '<td valign="top">Nice choice of music. LOL  This is great.</td>', 'Nice choice of music. LOL  This is great.', '2012-07-18 00:38:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820115, 1025426, 112828, '<td valign="top">Not a bad image, but I''m afraid that the dings/scratches/etc kinda spoil the whole "high technology" feel of this one.  The other issue as I see it is the way the door overhangs the wheelwell, it would be nice if it had extended down into the black void more, or if it had stayed entirely within the bounds of the body.  Either could have helped this image I think.<br/> <br/>In any case, still a nice example of technology, and a reasonably well done and processed image.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-07-23 00:15:23.</i></td>', 'Not a bad image, but I''m afraid that the dings/scratches/etc kinda spoil the whole "high technology" feel of this one.  The other issue as I see it is the way the door overhangs the wheelwell, it would be nice if it had extended down into the black void more, or if it had stayed entirely within the bounds of the body.  Either could have helped this image I think. In any case, still a nice example of technology, and a reasonably well done and processed image.', '2012-07-18 00:51:25.000000', '2012-07-23 01:15:23.000000', 1),
(6820116, 1025892, 112828, '<td valign="top">I find that shooting stuff like this is hard with anything but new units or really really worn units, as something like these that have been used a little, but not much, gives the contacts unattractive wear and marks.  A bit of cloning could have helped.  I also think a closer crop rotated to level would have been nicer..  Actually I''d like to have just seen a macro of the gold contacts, the pattern on those is great!  Love the contrast of straight lines and curves.</td>', 'I find that shooting stuff like this is hard with anything but new units or really really worn units, as something like these that have been used a little, but not much, gives the contacts unattractive wear and marks.  A bit of cloning could have helped.  I also think a closer crop rotated to level would have been nicer..  Actually I''d like to have just seen a macro of the gold contacts, the pattern on those is great!  Love the contrast of straight lines and curves.', '2012-07-18 00:51:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820118, 1025862, 112828, '<td valign="top">water drops are awesome looking.  But... This isn''t water drops.  So.. What do I see...  Honestly?  I''m left wondering if you wanted to try the water drop thing and just failed at it?  Sorry to say, but the concept could have been expressed in so many ways, why this mess of partially evaporated water.<br/> <br/>But then wait!  I look at this more and notice that the "water" seems to be alcohol that is burning..  Ok.. Kinda cool... And I like the orange coloration of the image too...  But.. Yeah, sorry, but... I still just don''t love the image!  My sincerest apologies.  But it does make me want to see this done with droplets of burning liquid - just have to be darn short between lighting and shooting.</td>', 'water drops are awesome looking.  But... This isn''t water drops.  So.. What do I see...  Honestly?  I''m left wondering if you wanted to try the water drop thing and just failed at it?  Sorry to say, but the concept could have been expressed in so many ways, why this mess of partially evaporated water. But then wait!  I look at this more and notice that the "water" seems to be alcohol that is burning..  Ok.. Kinda cool... And I like the orange coloration of the image too...  But.. Yeah, sorry, but... I still just don''t love the image!  My sincerest apologies.  But it does make me want to see this done with droplets of burning liquid - just have to be darn short between lighting and shooting.', '2012-07-18 00:52:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820119, 1025846, 112828, '<td valign="top">Ahh... Steven King.  How wonderfully dark..  I don''t LOVE the books you''ve chosen, but I don''t hate them either..  Neat shot and good illustration of the contrast between the early technology of the printing press vs the modern e-book.</td>', 'Ahh... Steven King.  How wonderfully dark..  I don''t LOVE the books you''ve chosen, but I don''t hate them either..  Neat shot and good illustration of the contrast between the early technology of the printing press vs the modern e-book.', '2012-07-18 00:52:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820121, 1025847, 112828, '<td valign="top">Cool image, but why did you choose to crop it this way?  And why can''t I see the entire front end loader - the bucket is the best bit of that one!<br/> <br/>I think a bit more of the water in the pit and a bit more of the arm of the excavator would have been nice.<br/> <br/>Processing is fine here, but I think it could have been pushed a bit further, but no more sharpening, you pretty much just nailed that.</td>', 'Cool image, but why did you choose to crop it this way?  And why can''t I see the entire front end loader - the bucket is the best bit of that one! I think a bit more of the water in the pit and a bit more of the arm of the excavator would have been nice. Processing is fine here, but I think it could have been pushed a bit further, but no more sharpening, you pretty much just nailed that.', '2012-07-18 00:53:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820122, 1025884, 112828, '<td valign="top">I don''t like the cross-processing look. I don''t like the composition.  I don''t like the image.<br/> <br/>But I really do like the concept.  I think the contrast between the old well windmill and the new power-generating windmills is great.  Wish the execution had been better, but I think the concept is very nice and carries a good story.</td>', 'I don''t like the cross-processing look. I don''t like the composition.  I don''t like the image. But I really do like the concept.  I think the contrast between the old well windmill and the new power-generating windmills is great.  Wish the execution had been better, but I think the concept is very nice and carries a good story.', '2012-07-18 00:53:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820124, 1025836, 112828, '<td valign="top">Hmm...  I find myself more interested in the haybales in the background.<br/> <br/>Frankly, it strikes me as a simple snapshot, processing isn''t bad, it isn''t great, but not bad...  The composition is OK(holy unlevel horizon Batman!), might have been able to do a bit better, but it works.  My issue is that this doesn''t really say technology, nor does it tell me you planned this out and made the best effort you could... I''ll predict a lower mid pack finish.</td>', 'Hmm...  I find myself more interested in the haybales in the background. Frankly, it strikes me as a simple snapshot, processing isn''t bad, it isn''t great, but not bad...  The composition is OK(holy unlevel horizon Batman!), might have been able to do a bit better, but it works.  My issue is that this doesn''t really say technology, nor does it tell me you planned this out and made the best effort you could... I''ll predict a lower mid pack finish.', '2012-07-18 00:53:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820127, 1025777, 112828, '<td valign="top">A nice piece of technology for sure.  I''m guessing this will finish mid pack, as it doesn''t really pop, but it''s within reason for the challenge, and the processing is ok as well.</td>', 'A nice piece of technology for sure.  I''m guessing this will finish mid pack, as it doesn''t really pop, but it''s within reason for the challenge, and the processing is ok as well.', '2012-07-18 00:53:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820129, 1025065, 112828, '<td valign="top">Love these old windowed chips...  I have a few in my collection, mostly old BIOSes.  I do wish that you had gotten more of the whole thing in focus, but I can see that his was probably a very intentional decision, so I''ll assume that you''re showing me just what you want to show me... I just love it less than I would if more was in focus I think.</td>', 'Love these old windowed chips...  I have a few in my collection, mostly old BIOSes.  I do wish that you had gotten more of the whole thing in focus, but I can see that his was probably a very intentional decision, so I''ll assume that you''re showing me just what you want to show me... I just love it less than I would if more was in focus I think.', '2012-07-18 00:53:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820130, 1025828, 112828, '<td valign="top">This should finish near or at the top..  Great concept and shoot...  I don''t think you conveyed the idea of technology quite as clearly as I would have liked, but, it''s still a really nice shot with excellent execution.  (and one heck of a patient dog!)</td>', 'This should finish near or at the top..  Great concept and shoot...  I don''t think you conveyed the idea of technology quite as clearly as I would have liked, but, it''s still a really nice shot with excellent execution.  (and one heck of a patient dog!)', '2012-07-18 00:53:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820131, 1025893, 112828, '<td valign="top">:) Makes me miss my old Droid 2..  Loved that phone.<br/> <br/>Shot is ok, concept is ok.  Don''t know that it screams technology, but the concept carries with the help of context.</td>', ':) Makes me miss my old Droid 2..  Loved that phone. Shot is ok, concept is ok.  Don''t know that it screams technology, but the concept carries with the help of context.', '2012-07-18 00:53:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820133, 1025773, 112828, '<td valign="top">Cool.  That''s absolutely some high tech stuff.  I like the shot overall, but I think a tighter crop may have worked better, I really don''t actually need to see the entire bike and the track.</td>', 'Cool.  That''s absolutely some high tech stuff.  I like the shot overall, but I think a tighter crop may have worked better, I really don''t actually need to see the entire bike and the track.', '2012-07-18 00:54:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820135, 1025657, 112828, '<td valign="top">Interesting.  I don''t love it, but I think you did an OK job with this.</td>', 'Interesting.  I don''t love it, but I think you did an OK job with this.', '2012-07-18 00:54:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820138, 1025843, 112828, '<td valign="top">hmm.  Clean, detailed and well set up...  I like it, but for whatever reason, I just don''t love it.....  So, am I looking through a bit of film in the foreground here?  I recognize the USB stick, but I can''t figure out what the heck that colorful bit is under the use?  Maybe a phone?  dunno.</td>', 'hmm.  Clean, detailed and well set up...  I like it, but for whatever reason, I just don''t love it.....  So, am I looking through a bit of film in the foreground here?  I recognize the USB stick, but I can''t figure out what the heck that colorful bit is under the use?  Maybe a phone?  dunno.', '2012-07-18 00:54:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820141, 1025874, 112828, '<td valign="top">Cool!  This worked out pretty ok, I don''t know if I quite ''get'' what you''re saying here, but the look, feel, crop, execution, processing, etc are all spot-on.  I expect to see this one near the top.</td>', 'Cool!  This worked out pretty ok, I don''t know if I quite ''get'' what you''re saying here, but the look, feel, crop, execution, processing, etc are all spot-on.  I expect to see this one near the top.', '2012-07-18 00:55:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820145, 1025911, 112828, '<td valign="top">Awwww.  How cute.<br/> <br/>Seriously though, not a bad concept or execution...  I''m not head-over heals crazy about this, as it just feels like a good stock image, but that''s ok, as I do think you met the challenge well, and expect to see this one near the top of the pack.</td>', 'Awwww.  How cute. Seriously though, not a bad concept or execution...  I''m not head-over heals crazy about this, as it just feels like a good stock image, but that''s ok, as I do think you met the challenge well, and expect to see this one near the top of the pack.', '2012-07-18 00:55:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820146, 1025767, 112828, '<td valign="top">Oh, how I wish that spark were blue, what possessed you to make the color such that that spark couldn''t shine through?</td>', 'Oh, how I wish that spark were blue, what possessed you to make the color such that that spark couldn''t shine through?', '2012-07-18 00:55:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820149, 1025716, 112828, '<td valign="top">Cool... I love old typewriters, took me a while to restore it but my old Royal works like a champ now - the biggest problem is finding ribbons! :)  <br/> <br/>The image is pretty ok - love the setup with crumpled paper and coffee/cigs..  Looks pretty much spot on for the concept of "yesterday''s technology"..</td>', 'Cool... I love old typewriters, took me a while to restore it but my old Royal works like a champ now - the biggest problem is finding ribbons! :)   The image is pretty ok - love the setup with crumpled paper and coffee/cigs..  Looks pretty much spot on for the concept of "yesterday''s technology"..', '2012-07-18 00:56:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820161, 1025630, 112828, '<td valign="top">Very nice.  I think the crop should have eliminated the right hand lower corner, as it''s fairly distracting.  Otherwise, really excellent gradient and shot..  I expect to see this float towards the top.</td>', 'Very nice.  I think the crop should have eliminated the right hand lower corner, as it''s fairly distracting.  Otherwise, really excellent gradient and shot..  I expect to see this float towards the top.', '2012-07-18 00:58:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820168, 1025825, 112828, '<td valign="top">Long exposures are wonderful, when there is a reason for it...  Here the only real reason is to make the car lights streak.  I would have probably liked this better from the opposite side of the overpass.  The star-bursts of light in the background are stellar, and I do like the overall feel, I''m afraid you just didn''t quite get the best out of this.</td>', 'Long exposures are wonderful, when there is a reason for it...  Here the only real reason is to make the car lights streak.  I would have probably liked this better from the opposite side of the overpass.  The star-bursts of light in the background are stellar, and I do like the overall feel, I''m afraid you just didn''t quite get the best out of this.', '2012-07-18 00:58:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820322, 1025828, 117037, '<td valign="top">Love this one...art of techno 10.</td>', 'Love this one...art of techno 10.', '2012-07-18 04:35:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820327, 1025595, 117037, '<td valign="top">Great work nice shot 10.</td>', 'Great work nice shot 10.', '2012-07-18 04:58:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820574, 1025907, 112828, '<td valign="top">Oh.  I see.  I think you''ve used the flash to show me something of the interior of your house and some sort of railing outside... So mostly I''m getting the flash.  And what the heck is a Healight?  <br/> <br/>I suspect you may trying for a brown.  I''m afraid that I must assist you in such an achievement.</td>', 'Oh.  I see.  I think you''ve used the flash to show me something of the interior of your house and some sort of railing outside... So mostly I''m getting the flash.  And what the heck is a Healight?   I suspect you may trying for a brown.  I''m afraid that I must assist you in such an achievement.', '2012-07-18 10:59:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820575, 1025912, 112828, '<td valign="top">So... you umm. flipped an overexposed photo of a dock 180 degrees, did some processing and submitted it?  What were you trying to say?  What was the idea you were trying to convey?  I don''t know, forgive me but I''m failing to understand the image.</td>', 'So... you umm. flipped an overexposed photo of a dock 180 degrees, did some processing and submitted it?  What were you trying to say?  What was the idea you were trying to convey?  I don''t know, forgive me but I''m failing to understand the image.', '2012-07-18 11:00:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820577, 1025870, 112828, '<td valign="top">I like this, sorta...  Mostly my issue is that the processing is really rough - too much high-radius contrast (structure), and too much saturation/contrast.  I''m afraid that the image just feels blotchy and overcooked.</td>', 'I like this, sorta...  Mostly my issue is that the processing is really rough - too much high-radius contrast (structure), and too much saturation/contrast.  I''m afraid that the image just feels blotchy and overcooked.', '2012-07-18 11:00:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820578, 1025605, 112828, '<td valign="top">Strange.  I don''t know that it screams technology, but it''s not bad either.  My concern is the overall composition, why is this laid out like it is, why not symmetrical?  Why not more context?</td>', 'Strange.  I don''t know that it screams technology, but it''s not bad either.  My concern is the overall composition, why is this laid out like it is, why not symmetrical?  Why not more context?', '2012-07-18 11:00:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820581, 1025751, 112828, '<td valign="top">I genuinely hope this ends up at the bottom of the pack.. Why in the heck would you do this to an image?  The whole thing has become a eye gouging nightmare because of the processing.  <br/> <br/>The simple save here would have been to simply convert this to B&amp;W, that would have taken away almost all of the eye-gouging aspects. I probably would have loved this as a super-low key image, perhaps if you had just cranked down the ISO and shot somewhat fast, then left me with an image of highlight and deep blacks, I probably would have preferred it...  All personal preference really, but bright pinks and greens with lots of blur and grain isn''t my thing. :)</td>', 'I genuinely hope this ends up at the bottom of the pack.. Why in the heck would you do this to an image?  The whole thing has become a eye gouging nightmare because of the processing.   The simple save here would have been to simply convert this to B&W, that would have taken away almost all of the eye-gouging aspects. I probably would have loved this as a super-low key image, perhaps if you had just cranked down the ISO and shot somewhat fast, then left me with an image of highlight and deep blacks, I probably would have preferred it...  All personal preference really, but bright pinks and greens with lots of blur and grain isn''t my thing. :)', '2012-07-18 11:04:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820583, 1025639, 112828, '<td valign="top">About the same as the other windmill shot.  Not great, but a good try.<br/> <br/>For me the image lacks richness, the corn just seems to lack depth and feels over processed...  *shrug*  You probably didn''t really do too much editing, it''s just that the corn ended up too sharp with a bit too much green, and not quite enough yellow. (the yellow is more of a pale straw color, I know it''s probably pretty accurate, but this image could have popped nicely with the yellows cranked up a bit more)</td>', 'About the same as the other windmill shot.  Not great, but a good try. For me the image lacks richness, the corn just seems to lack depth and feels over processed...  *shrug*  You probably didn''t really do too much editing, it''s just that the corn ended up too sharp with a bit too much green, and not quite enough yellow. (the yellow is more of a pale straw color, I know it''s probably pretty accurate, but this image could have popped nicely with the yellows cranked up a bit more)', '2012-07-18 11:06:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820584, 1025885, 112828, '<td valign="top">I see what you were trying to do.  I''m fear that I must tell you though - for me, you''ve failed to tie the title to the image that''s a ball, not a web...   And the image itself isn''t really telling me anything of technology.  Plus its'' a bit blurry....  Dunno, sorry, but this isn''t doing much for me at all, despite the fact that I really, really want to like it, the thumbnail is much better than the full-size.</td>', 'I see what you were trying to do.  I''m fear that I must tell you though - for me, you''ve failed to tie the title to the image that''s a ball, not a web...   And the image itself isn''t really telling me anything of technology.  Plus its'' a bit blurry....  Dunno, sorry, but this isn''t doing much for me at all, despite the fact that I really, really want to like it, the thumbnail is much better than the full-size.', '2012-07-18 11:08:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820585, 1025782, 112828, '<td valign="top">Despite the cartoonish feel, the processing is actually quite well done.  My question to you is "how does this convey technology to the viewer?"  I don''t really read "technology" in this photo... Overall it''s pretty good, but borders on DNMC/snapshot.   I think you''ll finish towards the top of the middle.</td>', 'Despite the cartoonish feel, the processing is actually quite well done.  My question to you is "how does this convey technology to the viewer?"  I don''t really read "technology" in this photo... Overall it''s pretty good, but borders on DNMC/snapshot.   I think you''ll finish towards the top of the middle.', '2012-07-18 11:09:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820586, 1025831, 112828, '<td valign="top">Hmm...  Too much negative space. Mostly OOF, point of interest isn''t that interesting, and the image doesn''t really convey "technology"... More like "gadgetry"...</td>', 'Hmm...  Too much negative space. Mostly OOF, point of interest isn''t that interesting, and the image doesn''t really convey "technology"... More like "gadgetry"...', '2012-07-18 11:09:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820587, 1025880, 112828, '<td valign="top">I have yet to see a good shot of this subject.  Sorry, but it''s a good concept, however this particular subject has almost become the unicorn of photography.</td>', 'I have yet to see a good shot of this subject.  Sorry, but it''s a good concept, however this particular subject has almost become the unicorn of photography.', '2012-07-18 11:09:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820591, 1025855, 112828, '<td valign="top">Overprocessed. Like crazy. That is all.<br/> <br/>The biggest give away on the crazy processing here is the halos around the trees from tonemapping the image.<br/> <br/>My suggestion for next time would be to separate the image into two halves, one the sky half, the other the ground and building, and adjust each separately, I would also suggest cutting back on the tonemapping, it''s an awesome tool when used correctly, but a little goes quite a long way. :)</td>', 'Overprocessed. Like crazy. That is all. The biggest give away on the crazy processing here is the halos around the trees from tonemapping the image. My suggestion for next time would be to separate the image into two halves, one the sky half, the other the ground and building, and adjust each separately, I would also suggest cutting back on the tonemapping, it''s an awesome tool when used correctly, but a little goes quite a long way. :)', '2012-07-18 11:12:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820594, 1025553, 112828, '<td valign="top">Oh, so mom bought a new video card huh?  So you thought maybe you should enter a snapshot of her trying to install it into a photo contest...  Surely you didn''t expect to do well?<br/> <br/>Technically, it''s sharp-ish, but it seems that the best focus in the image is on the dell logo on the motherboard.  The story lacks, the composition is not great at all...  *shrug*  Good try, but you''re gonna need to put more thought into composition and execution.<br/> <br/>Personally, I would have loved to have just seen a nice macro detail shot of that beautiful card and heatsink.</td>', 'Oh, so mom bought a new video card huh?  So you thought maybe you should enter a snapshot of her trying to install it into a photo contest...  Surely you didn''t expect to do well? Technically, it''s sharp-ish, but it seems that the best focus in the image is on the dell logo on the motherboard.  The story lacks, the composition is not great at all...  *shrug*  Good try, but you''re gonna need to put more thought into composition and execution. Personally, I would have loved to have just seen a nice macro detail shot of that beautiful card and heatsink.', '2012-07-18 11:13:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820595, 1025904, 112828, '<td valign="top">It''s red.  It''s Yamaha... It''s over processed like hell.<br/> <br/>*shrug* not bad, not great. Best of the worst I fear.</td>', 'It''s red.  It''s Yamaha... It''s over processed like hell. *shrug* not bad, not great. Best of the worst I fear.', '2012-07-18 11:13:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820596, 1025891, 112828, '<td valign="top">Meh. Monorail. Walt Disney World... Meh.  I think this just comes off as a family vacation snapshot as it fails entirely to convey "technology" to me as a concept.</td>', 'Meh. Monorail. Walt Disney World... Meh.  I think this just comes off as a family vacation snapshot as it fails entirely to convey "technology" to me as a concept.', '2012-07-18 11:13:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820597, 1025890, 112828, '<td valign="top">Pixels.  Water, colored squares. Not bad, but also not processed very well.  *shrug*... I hope it does ok, but I don''t love it either.</td>', 'Pixels.  Water, colored squares. Not bad, but also not processed very well.  *shrug*... I hope it does ok, but I don''t love it either.', '2012-07-18 11:14:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820599, 1025789, 112828, '<td valign="top">Oh.  Is it?<br/> <br/>Processing isn''t bad actually, the subtle shadows and mountains/plants is really nice in truth.   But despite that fact, the composition/execution/concept and communication of "technology" all are lacking for me.</td>', 'Oh.  Is it? Processing isn''t bad actually, the subtle shadows and mountains/plants is really nice in truth.   But despite that fact, the composition/execution/concept and communication of "technology" all are lacking for me.', '2012-07-18 11:14:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820601, 1025878, 112828, '<td valign="top">Yes... It''s a sign.  There''s technology everywhere, but you''ve failed to draw me to it.  Not at all a bad street shot though on it''s own merit.</td>', 'Yes... It''s a sign.  There''s technology everywhere, but you''ve failed to draw me to it.  Not at all a bad street shot though on it''s own merit.', '2012-07-18 11:15:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820602, 1025393, 112828, '<td valign="top">The birds help...  The unlevel horizon and flat processing doesn''t.</td>', 'The birds help...  The unlevel horizon and flat processing doesn''t.', '2012-07-18 11:15:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820603, 1025823, 112828, '<td valign="top">I really like this one... I see a figure in the corner, with an aliens face, Alfred Hitchcock and a Russian man with a boxers nose...  The image conveys a room, a face, human and beast...  This image is alive with intrigue and mystery, and while it doesn''t say a thing related to technology to me, I still love it very much...  <br/> <br/>I think I''m going to favorite this and vote it low, just as things should be.</td>', 'I really like this one... I see a figure in the corner, with an aliens face, Alfred Hitchcock and a Russian man with a boxers nose...  The image conveys a room, a face, human and beast...  This image is alive with intrigue and mystery, and while it doesn''t say a thing related to technology to me, I still love it very much...   I think I''m going to favorite this and vote it low, just as things should be.', '2012-07-18 11:15:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820604, 1025476, 112828, '<td valign="top">Hmm...  I assume you wanted the high-key look here?  Most of the image is blown out, which isn''t bad overall, but I would have liked to have kept some details in the white....  Composition leaves me wanting here, I wish I could see the bottom of that net, and that the town wasn''t visible to the left... Also wish I could see more of the wheelhouse.</td>', 'Hmm...  I assume you wanted the high-key look here?  Most of the image is blown out, which isn''t bad overall, but I would have liked to have kept some details in the white....  Composition leaves me wanting here, I wish I could see the bottom of that net, and that the town wasn''t visible to the left... Also wish I could see more of the wheelhouse.', '2012-07-18 11:16:22.000000', NULL, 1),
