(6820901, 1025753, 112828, '<td valign="top">Hmm...  What an interesting image.  Why is a fellow that old wearing a tie?  Why does he have a smart phone?  Is he still working?  Is he just hip? what''s the story?  I love it!  Looks like some sort of national or state park.</td>', 'Hmm...  What an interesting image.  Why is a fellow that old wearing a tie?  Why does he have a smart phone?  Is he still working?  Is he just hip? what''s the story?  I love it!  Looks like some sort of national or state park.', '2012-07-18 19:46:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820902, 1025604, 112828, '<td valign="top">Lensbaby?<br/> <br/>I think that this is one of the rare shots where a lensbaby really works well for the image and it''s needs.  I don''t love the image really, but I don''t hate it either, it certainly speaks of technology and changes.. At the same time, this isn''t really a killer photo, it''s just a solid shot.  I think you''ll probably score lower than you deserve, but I''m still only giving it a 6, as there''s just nothing here that really compels me.</td>', 'Lensbaby? I think that this is one of the rare shots where a lensbaby really works well for the image and it''s needs.  I don''t love the image really, but I don''t hate it either, it certainly speaks of technology and changes.. At the same time, this isn''t really a killer photo, it''s just a solid shot.  I think you''ll probably score lower than you deserve, but I''m still only giving it a 6, as there''s just nothing here that really compels me.', '2012-07-18 19:50:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820903, 1025900, 112828, '<td valign="top">heh... multitech...  Not bad.<br/> <br/>I like the overall image, exposure is good, composition and subject are interesting, and I like the illustration of the fact that not all technology really HAS to be human, even if we choose to regularly label it as such.<br/> <br/>I''m not sure about the grain, and I probably would have loved the bright colors, but, still, this image is worthy of a 7 in my book.</td>', 'heh... multitech...  Not bad. I like the overall image, exposure is good, composition and subject are interesting, and I like the illustration of the fact that not all technology really HAS to be human, even if we choose to regularly label it as such. I''m not sure about the grain, and I probably would have loved the bright colors, but, still, this image is worthy of a 7 in my book.', '2012-07-18 19:52:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820905, 1025841, 112828, '<td valign="top">My apologies for saying so, but I simply don''t like the angle here, and don''t really see the heavy tie in with technology..  It''s a good try, but for me this just comes off as a blatant shoehorn that could have been shot from a more intriguing angle.  Oh, and if you''re gonna do this sort of set up shot, you should clean your sensor and wash the car.. :) The lower right hand corner in particular shows some dust.. I do recognize that some of the blotchyness is just light from the canopy, but there are some specs here and there that really do detract, if they are paint chips and you couldn''t have washed them off, the cloning tool would have worked..<br/> <br/>Honestly, if it was my shot, I probably would have went a bit further and selected the ligher/mottled gray area and used the healing tool along with the blur tool to soften and smooth the entire thing out.</td>', 'My apologies for saying so, but I simply don''t like the angle here, and don''t really see the heavy tie in with technology..  It''s a good try, but for me this just comes off as a blatant shoehorn that could have been shot from a more intriguing angle.  Oh, and if you''re gonna do this sort of set up shot, you should clean your sensor and wash the car.. :) The lower right hand corner in particular shows some dust.. I do recognize that some of the blotchyness is just light from the canopy, but there are some specs here and there that really do detract, if they are paint chips and you couldn''t have washed them off, the cloning tool would have worked.. Honestly, if it was my shot, I probably would have went a bit further and selected the ligher/mottled gray area and used the healing tool along with the blur tool to soften and smooth the entire thing out.', '2012-07-18 19:55:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820906, 1025820, 112828, '<td valign="top">Hmm...   Feels contrived.  I don''t care for it, but it does say "technology" at least.</td>', 'Hmm...   Feels contrived.  I don''t care for it, but it does say "technology" at least.', '2012-07-18 19:57:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820907, 1025801, 112828, '<td valign="top">Hmm... So this is a picture of your speedometer at night while you''re doing 70mph?  Not exactly great planning there, not great planning on the shot and execution, not great planning on the life safety and risk management front either...  As for the image?  I like the crop... but it looks blotchy, pixelated and badly processed.  I''m sorry, but you''re gonna have to work harder to win me over.</td>', 'Hmm... So this is a picture of your speedometer at night while you''re doing 70mph?  Not exactly great planning there, not great planning on the shot and execution, not great planning on the life safety and risk management front either...  As for the image?  I like the crop... but it looks blotchy, pixelated and badly processed.  I''m sorry, but you''re gonna have to work harder to win me over.', '2012-07-18 19:58:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6820908, 1025068, 112828, '<td valign="top">I''ve looked at this four or five times now... And I keep just asking .. Why? <br/> <br/>I can''t help but notice that the frog looks like he needs to "Eat Mor Bugz" :)</td>', 'I''ve looked at this four or five times now... And I keep just asking .. Why?  I can''t help but notice that the frog looks like he needs to "Eat Mor Bugz" :)', '2012-07-18 19:59:33.000000', NULL, 1),
