(6821310, 1025804, 112828, '<td valign="top">Jeeze, that''s a hell of a machine!  I wish you had aligned the image with the tiles on the left hand side of the pic, but otherwise, it''s a very nice image, processing looks good and the subject is fascinating!</td>', 'Jeeze, that''s a hell of a machine!  I wish you had aligned the image with the tiles on the left hand side of the pic, but otherwise, it''s a very nice image, processing looks good and the subject is fascinating!', '2012-07-19 13:54:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6821313, 1025095, 112828, '<td valign="top">Hahn, is this you?  I don''t know that I see any cloud seeding here, but I''ll just trust you on that account.    Ok.  Sure it''s technology, but the image composition is just OK at best... If this is Richard''s image I''ll be just a little disappointed in that aspect of it.<br/> <br/>ETA: The issue, for me, with the composition is that the tree in the foreground blends too well with the background, and, again, for me, is somewhere in that nether-region where I feel there should either be more tree (vertically especially) or less tree.<br/> <br/>Again, though, I think it''s just how much that tree seems to blend in with the background, more tonal separation would have been very nice, or maybe more height.. I do like the cloud between it and the closest ridge, but.. *shrug*  Just ends up feeling like a decent composition overall in my mind.  (the peak is placed quite perfectly, and the crop aspect is great for this image too)</td>', 'Hahn, is this you?  I don''t know that I see any cloud seeding here, but I''ll just trust you on that account.    Ok.  Sure it''s technology, but the image composition is just OK at best... If this is Richard''s image I''ll be just a little disappointed in that aspect of it. ETA: The issue, for me, with the composition is that the tree in the foreground blends too well with the background, and, again, for me, is somewhere in that nether-region where I feel there should either be more tree (vertically especially) or less tree. Again, though, I think it''s just how much that tree seems to blend in with the background, more tonal separation would have been very nice, or maybe more height.. I do like the cloud between it and the closest ridge, but.. *shrug*  Just ends up feeling like a decent composition overall in my mind.  (the peak is placed quite perfectly, and the crop aspect is great for this image too)', '2012-07-19 13:56:11.000000', NULL, 1),
